From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase, kernel32, ntdll: CPU sets, NUMA nodes, ideal processors, priority boost

- SetThreadSelectedCpuSets and SetProcessDefaultCpuSets did nothing
  (games put their threads on CPU sets); GetThreadSelectedCpuSets and
  GetProcessDefaultCpuSets were missing. A selection is applied as the
  affinity and kept for reading back; an unknown CPU set id is refused.
- GetNumaNodeProcessorMask(Ex), GetNumaAvailableMemoryNode(Ex),
  GetNumaProcessorNodeEx and GetNumaProximityNode(Ex) failed with
  ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, GetNumaHighestNodeNumber said 0 and
  GetNumaProcessorNode said node 0 for every processor. They answer from
  the processor topology (GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx's NUMA nodes).
- SetThreadIdealProcessorEx failed, and the ideal processor was never
  kept. It is kept per thread; SetThreadIdealProcessor returns the
  previous one (MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS only asks), SetThreadIdealProcessorEx
  gives it back, GetThreadIdealProcessorEx reads it.
- Set/GetProcessPriorityBoost and Set/GetThreadPriorityBoost kept
  nothing. They are kept; a thread follows its process's setting until it
  sets its own.

Wine's kernel32 thread tests: the three priority boost checks marked
todo_wine pass now and are no longer marked; no new failures.

Gate: test/cpusets-gate.sh. Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_CPU_SETS,
SG_MUTANT_NO_NUMA (kernelbase/memory.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_IDEAL_PROCESSOR
(ntdll/unix/thread.c).
